// ATT&CK: execution, T1059
// Description: Detects the presence of the keywords "Wscript", "Shell" and "Run" in the command, which could
//   indicate a suspicious activity
// False positives:
//   - Inline scripting can be used by some rare third party applications or administrators. Investigate and apply additional filters accordingly
// References:
//   - https://web.archive.org/web/20220830122045/http://blog.talosintelligence.com/2022/08/modernloader-delivers-multiple-stealers.html
//   - https://blog.talosintelligence.com/modernloader-delivers-multiple-stealers-cryptominers-and-rats/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ad147b5514596e70f2782769d9833046b7c8e12b/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_mshta_inline_vbscript.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "Wscript." and ProcessCommandLine contains ".Shell" and ProcessCommandLine contains ".Run"
